SUMMARY:Nisarg Shah John Coltrane Celebration
LOCATION:Temple Performing Arts Center\, 1837 N. Broad Street\, Philadelpia
 \, PA 19121
DESCRIPTION:Nisarg Shah\, a Temple University senior pursuing a degree in J
 azz Studies\, leads an all-Philadelphia band in a free performance in the 
 Ruddick Jazz Café in the main lobby of the Temple Performing Arts Center.
  The performance celebrates John Coltrane’s centennial and the 60th anni
 versary of Coltrane’s “Offering: Live at Temple University”. Nisarg 
 Shah is joined by Dylan Band\, Tim Brey\, Sam Harris and Wayne Smith\, Jr.
  The performance is scheduled directly before Ravi Coltrane performs in Of
 fering…\n\nSource: Jazz Philadelphia\nEvent page: https://ma.to/event/ni
 sarg-shah-jazz-performance-12-nov-2026
