SUMMARY:Spirits of Independence at Powel House
LOCATION:Powel House\, 244 S. 3rd St.\, Philadelphia\, PA\, 19106
DESCRIPTION:Join us in exploring early drink in Philadelphia with Spirits o
 f Independence. Porter was the brew of choice for many in the colonial era
 . The Powel family was connected to the most renowned brewer of porter of 
 the time\, Robert Hare\, who had married into the Willing family. Speaker 
 Steve Grasse is the author of Colonial Spirits: A Toast to our Drunken His
 tory\, and he’ll give a talk about the importance of porter in the colon
 ial era and the experience of brewing porter from a colonial recipe.…\n\
 nSource: Queen Village Neighbors Association\nEvent page: https://www.qvna
 .org/events/spirits-of-independence-at-powel-house
URL:https://www.qvna.org/events/spirits-of-independence-at-powel-house
CATEGORIES:Queen Village Neighbors Association
END:VEVENT
